### StayFinder API examples
### Replace the example email/password and IDs with your own test account and disposable test records.
### Do not put real passwords, tokens, cookies, or service-role keys in this file.
### REST Client should retain the session cookie received at login. Otherwise use the browser.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = test-account@example.test
@password = replace-with-test-password
@propertyId = replace-with-disposable-property-uuid
@bookingId = replace-with-disposable-booking-uuid

### Register test account — expected 201 (if confirmation is required, confirm before login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Login — expected 200 and session cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Invalid login — expected 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "incorrect-test-password"
}

### Current user — expected 200 when signed in, 401 after clearing the cookie
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### Logout — expected 200; /auth/me should then return 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### Public list — expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/

### Filters and ascending price sort — expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/?location=Oslo&maxprice=250&maxguests=2&sort=asc

### Descending price sort — expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/?sort=desc

### Missing property — expected 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Create a disposable property while signed in — expected 201; copy its returned UUID into @propertyId
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Disposable test stay",
  "description": "Temporary API test property",
  "location": "Oslo",
  "kind": "apartment",
  "max_guests": 2,
  "price_per_night": 200
}

### Invalid property — expected 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "x",
  "description": "x",
  "location": "Oslo",
  "kind": "apartment",
  "max_guests": 0,
  "price_per_night": 50
}

### Property details — expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}

### Update your disposable property — expected 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Disposable test stay updated"
}

### Sign in as another account; updating someone else's disposable property is expected 403.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should not update"
}

### Create a future booking for the disposable property — expected 201; copy its UUID into @bookingId
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guest_name": "Test Guest",
  "guest_email": "test-guest@example.test",
  "check_in": "2099-01-10",
  "check_out": "2099-01-12",
  "guests": 2
}

### Invalid email/guest count — expected 400 and no booking created
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guest_name": "Test Guest",
  "guest_email": "not-an-email",
  "check_in": "2099-01-10",
  "check_out": "2099-01-12",
  "guests": 0
}

### Past check-in — expected 400 and no booking created
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guest_name": "Test Guest",
  "guest_email": "test-guest@example.test",
  "check_in": "2000-01-10",
  "check_out": "2000-01-12",
  "guests": 1
}

### Visible bookings — expected 200 for the guest or property owner, 401 signed out
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}

### Update your own future booking — expected 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}/{{bookingId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guest_name": "Test Guest Updated"
}

### Invalid booking dates — expected 400 and unchanged booking
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}/{{bookingId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "check_in": "2099-01-12",
  "check_out": "2099-01-12"
}

### Attempt to set booking status through API — expected 400 and unchanged booking
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}/{{bookingId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "confirmed"
}

### Non-owner checks: sign in as another test account; PATCH is expected 403 and the booking stays unchanged.
### DELETE is also expected 403; only run this against the disposable booking above.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}/{{bookingId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guest_name": "Should not update"
}

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}/{{bookingId}}

### Sign back in as the booking guest, then delete the disposable future booking — expected 204.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/properties/{{propertyId}}/{{bookingId}}

### Past booking edit/delete return 400. Use an existing disposable past booking only; do not change real records.

### Delete the disposable property only after the test — expected 204; cascades its disposable bookings.
### Do not run against an existing property.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}

### Unauthenticated property/booking creation returns 401. Clear the REST Client cookie jar before testing.
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Disposable test stay",
  "description": "Temporary API test property",
  "location": "Oslo",
  "kind": "apartment",
  "max_guests": 2,
  "price_per_night": 200
}

### Supabase direct RLS/trigger checks require authenticated user tokens and are not performed by this file.
